<title>USA: U.S. Rentals Inc Q1 pro forma net rises.</title>
<headline>U.S. Rentals Inc Q1 pro forma net rises.</headline>
<dateline>MODESTO, Calif. 1997-04-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>Three months ended</p>
<p>						 March 31,	March 31,</p>
<p>							1996	     1997</p>
<p>Revenues:</p>
<p>   Rental revenue			     $50,181	  $65,330</p>
<p>   Rental equipment sales		     3,910	    7,201</p>
<p>   Merchandise sales			    4,552	    8,450</p>
<p>  Total revenues				 58,643	   80,981</p>
<p>Cost of revenues:</p>
<p>   Rental equipment expense		  12,093	   17,276</p>
<p>   Rental equipment depreciation	   11,957	   14,313</p>
<p>   Cost of equipment sales		    1,446	    3,385</p>
<p>   Cost of merchandise sales		  3,088	    6,494</p>
<p>   Direct operating expense		  15,797	   21,183</p>
<p>  Total cost of revenues		     44,381	   62,651</p>
<p>  Gross profit				   14,262	   18,330</p>
<p>Selling, general and</p>
<p>  administrative expense			6,692	    7,553</p>
<p>Non-rental depreciation and</p>
<p>  amortization				    1,995	    2,152</p>
<p>Termination cost of</p>
<p>  deferred compensation agreements	    --	    20,290</p>
<p>  Operating income (loss)		     5,575</p>
<p>	 (11,665)</p>
<p>Other income (expense)			    134</p>
<p>	    (473)</p>
<p>Interest expense, net</p>
<p>  of interest income			   (1,475)</p>
<p>	 (1,501)</p>
<p>Income (loss) before income taxes</p>
<p>    and extraordinary item		    4,234</p>
<p>	 (13,639)</p>
<p>Income tax expense				  (29)</p>
<p>	 (9,894)</p>
<p>Income (loss) before</p>
<p>    extraordinary item			  4,205</p>
<p>	 (23,533)</p>
<p>Extraordinary item, (loss on</p>
<p>extinguishment of debt less</p>
<p>applicable income tax</p>
<p>  benefit of $995)				  --</p>
<p>	   (1,511)</p>
<p>  Net income (loss)			    $4,205</p>
<p>$(25,044)</p>
<p>Pro forma net income data:</p>
<p>Pro forma income before income taxes     $5,709	   $8,549</p>
<p>Pro forma income tax expense		  2,298	    3,397</p>
<p>Pro forma net income			   $3,411	   $5,152</p>
<p>Pro forma net income per share		$0.11	    $0.17</p>
<p>Shares used in computing</p>
<p>   pro forma net income per share    30,748,975    30,748,975</p>
<p>Note: The pro forma results reflect income taxes as if the company had been a C-corporation for all periods and the recording of related deferred tax liabilities, and do not include the one-time $20,290 million 1997 charge relating to termination of deferred compensation agreements with certain employees, $2,506 million 1997 charge relating to the early extinguishment of debt, and $1,491 and $1,475 million of 1997 and 1996 interest expense as a result of reductions in indebtedness, respectively.  All charges relate to the termination of the company's S-corporation status and corporate reorganization in connection with its initial public offering on February 21, 1997.</p>
